<title>CROATIA: Croatia to sell property of Plitvice Park - paper.</title>
<headline>Croatia to sell property of Plitvice Park - paper.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia announced on Friday plans to sell real estate belonging to the Plitvice National Park, worth more than 14 million German marks.</p>
<p>In a paid advertisement in the Zagreb daily Vjesnik, the state-owned company Nacionalni Park &quot;Plitvicka Jezera&quot; said it wanted to sell some 34 properties in the mountainous Lika area of central Croatia.</p>
<p>The offer includes three hotels, including Hotel Javornik in Udbina, Hotel Maslenica near Zadar and Hotel Pljesivica in Korenica.</p>
<p>The National Park is also selling a number of shops and supermarkets, cafe bars, butcheries, warehouses, farms, stables, a pharmacy and a book store.</p>
<p>Institutions and individuals of Croatia are allowed to take part in the tender, opened till June 30.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb Newsroom, + 385 1 4557-075</p>
</text>
